---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Research">
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p>
    My main research is in gravitational-wave detection within the LIGO Scientific
    Collaboration, with a focus on low-latency signal processing. I also have prior
    work in statistical physics from my undergraduate years.
  </p>

  <h2>Gravitational-Wave Detection (LIGO)</h2>

  <div class="card-stack">
    <article class="project-card">
      <h3>Targeted Search for GstLAL</h3>
      <p>
        Co-architected the &ldquo;Targeted Search&rdquo; method for GstLAL, integrating
        electromagnetic-counterpart data as Bayesian priors. By concentrating sensitivity
        around joint multi-messenger candidates, the approach improves signal-detection
        sensitivity by roughly three orders of magnitude (~1000&times;) while keeping the
        same low-latency profile.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
      <h3>Intermediate-Mass Black Hole Search (GWTC-5)</h3>
      <p>
        Led the Intermediate-Mass Black Hole (IMBH) offline search for the GWTC-5
        production run. Refined background-noise estimation models, achieving a 13%
        improvement in noise-rejection accuracy over the previous baseline.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
      <h3>SGNL Pipeline — Parameter Estimation Review</h3>
      <p>
        Conducted parameter-estimation (PE) review for the SGNL pipeline. Optimized
        statistical estimators and improved P-P plot consistency and result reliability
        by 33%.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="project-card">
      <h3>GstLAL Pipeline Engineering</h3>
      <p>
        Maintain the GstLAL hybrid C++/Python pipeline, which processes terabytes of
        streaming detector data with sub-second latency to generate real-time
        gravitational-wave triggers.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Statistical Physics</h2>

  <div class="card-stack">
    <article class="project-card">
      <h3>Dynamics, Statistics, and Task Allocation of Foraging Ants</h3>
      <p class="role">First-author paper &middot; NTU, 2020 &ndash; 2022</p>
      <p>
        Developed an agent-based simulation of collective foraging combining MCMC with a
        custom random-walk algorithm. Code-level optimization and sampling improvements
        cut simulation runtime from days to hours (~50&times; speedup).
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
